.SH DIAGNOSTICS
On ending, each program returns a string called the
.IR "exit status" .
It is the argument of the program's call to
.IR wait (2)'s
.IR exits ,
or the text of the note that ended it.
The empty string means success.
A non-empty one says why the program failed,
in a few words a person can read.
